Assets of the subhalo-lensing part.

subhalo-lensing-data.js: generated by tasks/t10-subhalo-lensing/S1/make_data.py, a copy of
the "nr" (trimmed prod_n24 NR tracks, horizon radii; task t04-ringdown) and "wave" (unlensed
h_22 and the wave diffracted by a cored isothermal sphere, GLoW 0.1, Villarrubia-Rojo+
2409.04606, GPL-3.0-or-later; only its numerical output) entries of
slides/parts/gw-lensing/assets/gw-lensing-data.js (task t08-gw-lensing).

earth_apollo17_400.png: copy of slides/parts/gw-lensing/assets/earth_apollo17_400.png.
"The Blue Marble", NASA / Apollo 17 crew, 7 December 1972; public domain (NASA),
NASA GRIN GPN-2000-001138, via Wikimedia Commons. Cropped to the disk, 400x400.

goyal_l1_fit_decomposition.png: Goyal+ (2512.17631), figures/L1_data_plus_decomposition.pdf
from the arXiv source (lit_cache/arxiv-2512.17631-src.tar.gz), rasterised with
pdftoppm -r 400. GW231123 L1 data (cWB reconstruction) with the embedded point-lens best fit
and the unlensed best fit; decomposition into main image, secondary image, diffraction.

vujeva_fig3_lensing_rates.png: Vujeva+ (2608.07667) Fig. 3, figures/figure_3_lensing_rates.pdf
from the arXiv source (lit_cache/arxiv-2608.07667-src.tar.gz), rasterised with pdftoppm -r 300.
Detections against year: GW events, strongly lensed, and IMBH+GC lensed (well below 1).

goyal_source_posteriors.png, goyal_source_posteriors_legend.png: Goyal+ (2512.17631),
figures/systematics_hvr.pdf (1D posteriors of detector-frame chirp mass, q, chi_1, chi_2 for
unlensed, isolated and embedded point lens, three waveform models) rasterised with
pdftoppm -r 400, and figures/systematics_legend_horr_new_1-3.pdf rasterised at -r 400 and
cropped as in the paper (trim 20 pt left, 15 pt bottom: -x 111 -y 0 -W 2289 -H 317).
The Bayes-factor row on the slide is typed from the paper's Table I (table_1.tex), embedded
point lens: log10 B^L_U = 2.82 (NRSur), 5.0 (Phenom), 1.24 (SEOBNR).
